WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.220
- Your daughter is almost 16.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.580
- Yes.
- What's she like?

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:06.230
We have a 3, 5, 13, and 18-year-old, so.

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.840
- I mean, you lost me
after the second one.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.140
- Yeah, well, no, but a teenager,

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:11.973
that can be trying.

00:00:11.973 --> 00:00:14.644
- Oh, my God, just keep
us in your prayers.

00:00:14.644 --> 00:00:16.560
(Kelly laughs)
My daughter,

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.310
it's hard to watch yourself,

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.360
she's like, watching
now, that she's older,

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:22.470
it's like watching myself, it's scary.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:25.439
What I'm so grateful to God
for is that I am a woman,

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:28.029
And I can teach her how to be a woman.

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:30.080
(audience cheers)
Had I had a male child,

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.455
it would've been a little different.

00:00:31.455 --> 00:00:34.000
- Yeah.
- I was a single mom,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.330
which I did not expect to be.

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:37.720
I didn't have her until
I was 35 years old,

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:41.040
so had already had career
first and then kind of,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.360
you know, just got into motherhood

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.780
and I think it's been the most gratifying

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:48.290
and amazing, and just rocky road

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.040
that I've ever taken in my life,

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.100
but she's that one person that I would die

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.530
in a blink of an eye for.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.990
So it's motherhood first
and then everything else.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.040
- Yeah, there's so much love.
(audience clapping)

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.740
And then, sometimes, there's
so much dislike (laughs).

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.088
There's so much love but yeah,
- Oh, my god.

00:01:08.088 --> 00:01:09.751
- Sometimes I'm like,
- And you got four of them.

00:01:09.751 --> 00:01:10.840
- I love you, but I
don't like you right now,

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:15.020
so for your safety, you
should leave my presence.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.580
- That's because they
didn't know us before

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.295
we were moms, I keep telling her,

00:01:20.295 --> 00:01:23.447
I was like, "Yo, I used to be somebody

00:01:23.447 --> 00:01:25.810
"before I was your mother,

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.980
"and you might be meeting
this person real soon."

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:30.855
(audience laughing)

00:01:30.855 --> 00:01:31.688
- And you?

00:01:33.222 --> 00:01:35.308
- Do you wannna meet that person?

00:01:35.308 --> 00:01:37.040
- All right, take it
easy, take it easy there.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.370
- And it's like, "And
apologize for what you did

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:41.063
to my body, that's all I want".

00:01:41.973 --> 00:01:43.530
- It's stupid, I give it up to mothers,

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.580
God bless you, I think it's wonderful.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.420
- I love being a mother, I
never thought I'd be one.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:49.347
My mom is still like, "Oh,
my God, you have children

00:01:49.347 --> 00:01:50.297
"and a husband".

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.680
But Tichina, you've got a
way, this is my favorite thing

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:56.210
ever heard with parenting.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:02:00.430
You've got a way with your
daughter to kind of punish her,

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:01.960
and it deals with a cellphone.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.390
- Oh, most definitely,
we live in a day and age

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.610
where we all have cellphones, you know,

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:10.620
we are attached to our devices,

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:14.100
and I tried taking the
cellphone away from her,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.480
which, you know, it
wasn't really advantageous

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.090
for me, because she takes Uber sometimes,

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:20.460
we need the cellphone.

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.804
So okay, I'm gonna get you a flip phone.

00:02:22.804 --> 00:02:25.200
(audience laughs)
I got her a flip phone.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.390
And now, everything goes through my phone,

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.390
you know, so I know how to shut her down

00:02:30.493 --> 00:02:31.381
when I need to.

00:02:31.381 --> 00:02:33.280
There's a way of
punishing someone without,

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.080
you know, not having contact with them.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.910
We can still have contact,
but I had to give her

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.704
a flip phone, because it's
all the control I have.

00:02:39.704 --> 00:02:41.533
- You know, when she's with her friends,

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:43.996
and she pulls out her
Ferris Bueller phone.

00:02:45.054 --> 00:02:46.440
- Yeah, oh yeah, take
it back to the old days,

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:48.336
that's when mommy had a flip phone,

00:02:48.336 --> 00:02:49.857
you can have a flip phone too.

00:02:49.857 --> 00:02:51.750
- (Kelly laughs) Give her a beeper.

00:02:51.750 --> 00:02:52.900
I love you, oh, my God.

